  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 13/12/05, the erection of a single storey rear extension measuring 49.76 cubic metres was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because it does not extend between the house and the highway, is not above 4 m in height within 2 m of the boundary, does not increase the height of the house and does not, together with other extensions or outbuildings, take more than half the garden area.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
